      "scenario_id": "KA-01-bearing",
      "run_key": "master-tot-critic-on-run-1/1/KA-01-bearing",
      "expected_faults": [
        "bearing_degradation"
      ],
      "final_diagnosis": "CNC-02 has a developing mechanical fault, most consistent with bearing wear or imbalance: its vibration ran 4.16-4.58 mm/s over ticks 910-920 (E3) and tripped the 4.50 mm/s alarm twice, at tick 914 (4.58 mm/s) and tick 919 (4.51 mm/s) (E10). CNC-02 is the clear outlier: every other machine checked - CNC-01, CNC-03, CNC-04, CNC-05, CNC-06, CNC-08 - stays at or below 2.54 mm/s over the same window (E14-E20), so its 850 rpm setting and 50-57% load (E5, E13) do not explain the level and the nuisance-threshold hypothesis (H2) is contradicted. Temperature is flat at about 144-147 F through the window (E4), with no spike correlating with the alarm, so this is not a thermal issue. The readings are steadily elevated rather than erratic, which argues against a random sensor fault, but a biased CNC-02 vibration sensor (H3) cannot be ruled out without a second independent sensor (T3) or a longer upward trend (T1). Confidence: 0.78. To reach the 0.90 needed for an approved intervention, confirm with a second vibration sensor on CNC-02, a longer trend (ticks 850-920), or a physical inspection; if confirmed, replace_bearing would be the fix (about 45 ticks of downtime).",
